SIM-08: compare heads for level controls on reservoirs

controls() decides whether a tank-level control fires by comparing tank
volumes. tankvolume() returns Vmin for a reservoir (area 0) whatever the
head, so both volumes were equal and every BELOW and ABOVE control on a
reservoir fired at every time step. For a reservoir, compare its head
with the control grade instead.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply SIM-08_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/hydraul.c b/src/hydraul.c
index fa96868..14bd376 100755
--- a/src/hydraul.c
+++ b/src/hydraul.c
@@ -598,6 +598,14 @@ int  controls(Project *pr)
             vplus = ABS(hyd->NodeDemand[n]);
             v1 = tankvolume(pr,n - net->Njuncs,h);
             v2 = tankvolume(pr,n - net->Njuncs, control->Grade);
+
+            // A reservoir has no volume, so compare its head instead
+            if (net->Tank[n - net->Njuncs].A == 0.0)
+            {
+                v1 = h;
+                v2 = control->Grade;
+                vplus = 0.0;
+            }
             if (control->Type == LOWLEVEL && v1 <= v2 + vplus) reset = 1;
             if (control->Type == HILEVEL && v1 >= v2 - vplus)  reset = 1;
         }
